Notebook[{
Cell["Guard extraction over control flow \[LongDash] Findings (v0)", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"17348d1a-b849-47c5-94d1-70f18d458eb5"],

Cell["\<\
gtpyhop-diagnostics, commit dc3f852: an if is a guard only if every \
successful path passes it\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"827581fb-dd08-4a63-849c-c8f791714ddf"],

Cell["\<\
type: findings
topic: diagnostics_guard_cf
date: 2026-11-16
version: v0
prior-version: none (continues diagnostics_guard_nnf round 00, R6)
key-metric: unsound atoms over every action body of \[LessEqual] 6 \
statements: 0 (prior: 13,890 with the ast.walk reading)
decision-required: confirm\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"aa40c6c5-927f-4db7-8fe2-216d73d28e76"],

Cell["Headline Result", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"23ec3bcf-0f82-4030-b408-5504169ef126"],

Cell["\<\
metric:    unsound atoms extracted, every action body of \[LessEqual] 6 \
statements (if/else, loop, return state, return False, effect) over 3 tests
value:     0  (path-aware, dc3f852)
unit:      atoms
prior:     13,890 (ast.walk reading, 0.1.1)
direction: down\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"32e754cb-3142-46f3-b547-f6014cb18160"],

Cell["\<\
decision-required is confirm: file the control-flow issue together with \
dc3f852. The fix only removes atoms (R3, last column), the removal is proved \
sound for every program (R2), and the Python code computes exactly what the \
model proves (R5). Its cost is precision in two places: inside loops, and \
where the same test is read twice on a path (R4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e66599f2-0fae-4ba1-95f9-e0d86658e0a7"],

Cell["Model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c7882a06-64bd-40e6-9078-7c4b7e9816c9"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 proved that each guard's requirement splits into atoms soundly. This \
round asks which ifs have a requirement at all. explain_dead_end only \
analyses actions the planner recorded as not applicable (they returned False \
or None), so an atom is honest exactly when every other outcome implies it: \
success \[DoubleLongRightArrow] atom. 0.1.1 found guards with ast.walk and \
read every if as guarding the whole action. dc3f852 walks the statements \
backwards and keeps, as (if, polarity) pairs, the requirements every \
successful path passes. The reading of each if is unchanged; its atoms are \
kept only if that pair is in the set.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b988b648-04fc-4444-9189-907e5e4bbd88"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"statement\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"may succeed\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"required on every success\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"why\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"return state (any non-falsey return)\"\>", "\<\"yes\"\>", \
"\<\"nothing\"\>", "\<\"succeeds here, whatever came before\"\>"},
    {"\<\"return False / return None / return / raise\"\>", "\<\"no\"\>", "\<\
\"\[LongDash]\"\>", "\<\"cannot succeed\"\>"},
    {"\<\"if t: A else: B, A cannot succeed\"\>", "\<\"as B\"\>", "\<\"not t, \
plus what B needs\"\>", "\<\"every success goes through B\"\>"},
    {"\<\"if t: A else: B, B cannot succeed\"\>", "\<\"as A\"\>", "\<\"t, \
plus what A needs\"\>", "\<\"every success goes through A\"\>"},
    {"\<\"if t: A else: B, both can\"\>", "\<\"yes\"\>", "\<\"what both A and \
B need\"\>", "\<\"a success may take either branch\"\>"},
    {"\<\"loop, with, try: no success return inside\"\>", "\<\"as what \
follows\"\>", "\<\"what follows needs\"\>", "\<\"every success leaves it and \
continues\"\>"},
    {"\<\"loop, with, try: a success return inside\"\>", "\<\"yes\"\>", \
"\<\"nothing\"\>", "\<\"a success may end inside it\"\>"},
    {"\<\"anything else\"\>", "\<\"as what follows\"\>", "\<\"what follows \
needs\"\>", "\<\"falls through\"\>"},
    {"\<\"end of the function\"\>", "\<\"no\"\>", "\<\"\[LongDash]\"\>", \
"\<\"falls off: returns None\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.9]}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.2}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"fad18943-9752-41a6-a994-f69bbdb98431"],

Cell["\<\
Model syntax, inert so nothing simplifies before the rules see it: ok (return \
state), bail (return False, covering None, bare return and raise), eff (an \
effect), if[id, t, A, B], loop[id, A]. Tests are read on the state the action \
was called on, which is what explain_dead_end evaluates atoms against. A loop \
body runs on a fresh unknown c[id]: zero iterations, or at least one, which \
with tests read on the pre-state behaves as one.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f844c427-0610-4bbd-ae2e-ccdb0da329f7"],

Cell["Results Tables", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8a1bcada-b961-469a-8d0b-6b2b61b4975b"],

