Cell["Scope: what this does not prove", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2b0d0f53-346b-4364-8030-f20e28e50823"],

Cell["\<\
The bundled and corpus counts are measurements, made with \
diagnostics_guard_nnf/scripts/examples_diff.py and corpus.py and listed in \
the commit message, not computed here.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f140c56-afbb-4f7a-ab77-d6b3dd211870"],

Cell["\<\
Tests are read on the state the action was called on. A guard that reads \
state the action has already changed is a separate, older limitation, \
untouched here.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"cb76900f-1299-4a89-bd4d-44f399f6fa5f"],

Cell["\<\
The enumeration omits break, continue, while-else, with, try and match. R2 \
covers them through the compound rows; the property case in \
tools/diagnostics_guard_check.py executes generated bodies with loops and \
raise.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"16680915-f2f3-407f-aba9-8ab4269b979d"],

Cell["\<\
Diagnostics run after find_plan returns; none of this changes which plans are \
found.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0fb005c7-a125-4841-bbe6-213bab5c5f5b"],

